WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.801
-Our next guest is a very talented actor

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.267
and comedian you know from shows like

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.801
"The Mindy Project" and "Happy Endings."

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.701
He stars in "Who Invited Charlie?",

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.033
which is in theaters and on demand February 3rd.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.167
Let's take a look. -Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:14.400
Listen, I'm making some green smoothies for me and Max.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.868
You want one? -Oh, you know what? No.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.601
I'd actually rather have a big tall glass of warm piss.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.567
I said I'd rather have a tall glass of warm piss!

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.667
Did he not hear it?

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.200
-Really?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.734
-It's just a little hair of the dog.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.434
You don't have to be so judgy.

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.434
-Wait. Where did you even find the mixer for that?

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.701
-In your bar.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.734
-Oh, dude, that stuff's like three summers old.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.200
-Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. I guess that's why it's, like, kinda --

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.067
It has a fur.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.767
-Please wake back to the show our friend

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.434
Adam Pally, everybody.

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:44.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:51.367
♪♪

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:57.834
♪♪

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.033
Welcome!

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.100
-Thank you so much. So happy to be here.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.067
-This is a very wonderful COVID era film.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.734
You were here right before lockdown.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.834
-Yes. -And then how --

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.534
Did you manage to avoid COVID? How did you do?

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.701
-No, I've had all the COVIDs.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:18.033
I got the COVID ones.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.968
The COVID twos.

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.534
Then I waited online all night for the COVID threes.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.200
-And you got it? -Snagged 'em.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.801
Snagged 'em. -Early three.

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:29.267
-Yeah, and then my son gave me the COVID fours just as a gift.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:31.634
[ Laughter ] -Wow.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:34.400
They're going to, like, test your blood. Special guy.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.901
-Well, I have a little tip. I microdose COVID.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.601
A little bit of COVID every morning,

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.334
not too much that you feel the effects,

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.767
but enough to build up an immunity.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:48.167
-Oh, that's great.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.434
-Yeah, it's just -- if you take too much,

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.934
you do find yourself at work like,

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.367
"I can't breathe or smell."

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:56.234
But that's fine. You know, it's part of it.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.367
-You -- I've enjoyed talking to you

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.868
because I'm doing the same.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.434
You've got three New York City kids.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:02.634
-Yes.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:03.901
-Been a while since I last checked in.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.901
How has raising them in the city gone?

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.601
-You know, it's good.

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.767
I enjoy the stigma of New York City kids,

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.567
being that they're a little more mature

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:15.200
or they've seen more or gotten to know more.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.334
So I enjoy it.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:20.734
It is, like, sometimes jarring to me

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.334
as someone who also grew up in New York City.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.734
It was a very different New York City.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.467
But, like, my son the other day --

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:28.000
They called from school and they were like,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.367
"Cole, he has a fever. You got to come pick him up."

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.701
And I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.501
You know, ran to school, got him.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.300
And, you know, he had a fever,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.000
and they're so cuddly when they're sick, you know?

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.734
And he was like, "Thanks for picking me up, Dad."

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:42.133
And I was like, "You never have to worry about that, kiddo.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.701
Like, I'm here for you."

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.167
And he's like, "I'm a little hungry."

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:47.667
And I was like, "I'll get you whatever -- whatever you want.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.000
We'll get whatever -- whatever you want."

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.534
He's like, "For real, Dad?"

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.634
And I was like, "Buddy, yes. I'm here for you."

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.133
And he's like, "Can we get the baked crab hand roll

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.801
from Bond Street?"

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:07.167
-That's not the kind of New York kid you were, huh?

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.033
-No.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:12.601
First of all, I was like, "No.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.901
No. It's like $24.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:18.934
I didn't mean anything. I meant --"

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.567
I was like, "Be reasonable."

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.434
-Also, that's not a food when you're sick --

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.067
No one's like, "You want a crab roll?"

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.634
-Yeah, I was like, "Are you faking?"

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:27.634
I was like, "Come on. You want a baked crab roll?"

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:30.567
But he did. He ate two of them.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:33.367
And I found myself with an $80 Postmates order

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.400
at 2:00 in the afternoon.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.300
You're like, "Jesus. What happened here?"

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.100
-You appreciate this --

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.734
Or I should say, I appreciate this --

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:45.100
Having three kids, it's hard to keep up with everything.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.601
You do not like when people ask you,

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:48.934
"What are you watching?"

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.734
-I don't like that question.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:55.701
I find it to be, uh, rude.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.901
Because -- And not just because I have three children.

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.267
And the truth is, as you know,

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:01.267
you don't get to watch a lot of stuff.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.133
-Yeah. -If I get to watch maybe one,

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:07.601
two shows a year from beginning to end, that's like a lot.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:09.534
So I feel offended.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:12.167
And, frankly, maybe it's my age or whatever,

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.567
but I feel like a lot of the shows my friends

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.434
tell me they're seeing are made up.

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.000
It all sounds made up to me.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.934
-Okay. -Like, every show.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:25.734
And then you ask them who's in it, and it all sounds made up.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.200
It's like someone --

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.667
They're like, "What are you watching?"

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:29.901
Like, "Oh, what am I watching?

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:32.634
I don't know. 'Dream Catcher and the Salmon.'

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.000
You haven't seen that?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.167
It stars Chris O'Dowd and Patricia Heaton.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.601
It's on Epix.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.567
It's kind of a slow burn. You've got to stick with it."

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:48.100
Like, that sounds like it's a show, but it's not a show.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.567
-Now, you -- Don't take this the wrong way.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:52.067
You are in a show that seems like one of your made-up shows.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:55.400
-Yeah, I'm in an action show on Netflix

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.033
with Arnold Schwarzenegger. -Okay.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.734
Now, that sounds super made-up.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:00.133
-It sounds like I'm lying.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:03.400
Like, it sounds like -- But it's real. That's real!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.000
-And how was your time with Arnold Schwarzenegger?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.567
-Great. -Yeah?

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.801
-Yeah. He's amazing. He's like --

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:13.000
I would say, if any-- He's just a great guy.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.501
Like, he -- And everybody around him loves him.

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:20.601
And he's had the same team forever.

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:23.501
And I remember one day I was like,

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.434
"Arnold. God. Everybody loves you.

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:30.334
And they've been with you forever, and it's so --

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.167
And I kept going. He's like...

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:34.334
[as Schwarzenegger] "Of course. I am the best."

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.601
He looked at me like it was like,

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:42.067
"What are you talking about?

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.033
You talking about how I could not be the best?

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:45.868
Like, what is -- I'm the best."

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:47.801
I was like, "Oh, right."

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:51.000
Anything. It'd be like, "God, this coffee is so good."

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.868
He's like, "Of course it is."

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.734
-Did you do -- It's an action thing. Did you do action?

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.334
-Yeah, I did a little action. -Okay.

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:01.834
-My first day, I was a little nervous.

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:04.767
We were strapped together in a tandem parachute.

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:06.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.501
It was nerve-racking, you know.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:11.300
And, like, he smelled it on me right away.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.968
You know, I'm strapped to him.

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:15.300
And he's like, "This is your first time in a parachute?"

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:22.334
And I was like, "Uh, yeah. Yeah, Arnold."

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:27.434
And he turned to his team and he starts talking in Austrian.

00:06:27.434 --> 00:06:31.300
And he's like -- [ Imitating Austrian ]

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.033
...first time...

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:35.367
[ Grunts ]

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:37.634
And I'm like --

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:39.567
You know, for a Jew,

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:41.868
you start hearing Austrian, you're like...

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:49.300
You know? So I'm like, "What is --

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.834
What is happening?" So I'm like --

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:53.501
And they're all laughing.

00:06:53.501 --> 00:06:56.934
You know, everyone's like, "Ha, ha, ha!"

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:59.334
You know? And I was like --

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:01.567
"What's going on? Is everything okay?"

00:07:01.567 --> 00:07:03.901
And he's like, "Yeah, yeah."

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:06.834
And I was like, "Well, what did they say

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:09.567
when you said that I was nervous?"

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:10.934
And he's like -- [ Chuckles ]

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:13.100
"They said you're not gonna like it."

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.501
Like, that -- That's all they said?

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:20.834
The conversation went on for an hour!

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:24.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:26.300
But he's great.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.968
-Yeah. -He's great.

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:30.501
And I really, like -- I would tell everyone, like,

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:32.934
if you get the chance to spend time with him --

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:34.767
He does -- There is a thing that I would love to ask him

00:07:34.767 --> 00:07:36.567
because I never...

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:39.334
After I did it, I changed my Waze, you know...

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:41.033
-Yeah, yeah. -...to be Arnold's voice.

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:42.734
-Oh, your Waze. Okay. Gotcha. Your map.

00:07:42.734 --> 00:07:44.934
-Yeah. Because you can do that. You can move --

00:07:44.934 --> 00:07:47.501
And so after it, this will be fun and, like, remind me.

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:50.534
And so now I have Arnold telling me...

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:53.534
[as Schwarzenegger] "Turn left. I'm not kidding!"

00:07:53.534 --> 00:07:55.868
You know? Like, truly.

00:07:55.868 --> 00:07:58.801
You put in the destination, and he goes like,

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:00.801
"I'll be back, but first we'll get you

00:08:00.801 --> 00:08:02.834
to the Claridge House."

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:05.434
You know? And you're like, "Alright."

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:09.100
But lately I've noticed that his directions --

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.801
I don't know if he did this on purpose.

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:12.501
And if he did, he's a genius.

00:08:12.501 --> 00:08:16.133
He lau-- He kind of laughs in his direction.

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.701
So you don't know if you should believe him.

00:08:18.701 --> 00:08:20.267
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:23.100
So he'll be like, "Turn left."

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.968
And you'll be like...

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:28.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.634 --> 00:08:32.634
Or he'll be like, "Slow down. Speed camera ahead. Ha, ha."

00:08:32.634 --> 00:08:34.234
You're like...

00:08:34.234 --> 00:08:37.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:39.767
Is there a speed camera ahead?

00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:44.334
And I feel like he knew that because his voice is so strong

00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:45.934
that you're just gonna believe him.

00:08:45.934 --> 00:08:49.100
-Yeah. -So I feel like if --

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.567
I may be getting pranked

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:53.734
and, like, I'm driving everywhere like --

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:57.200
Both signals are on all the time, and I'm nervous.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.834
-Well, I want to say something that I mean genuinely.

00:08:58.834 --> 00:09:00.667
I really hope the show with you and Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:02.367
isn't made up.

00:09:02.367 --> 00:09:03.801
I hope it's a real thing. -No. I mean, I filmed it.

00:09:03.801 --> 00:09:07.667
So -- It could have been a fever dream. I mean --

00:09:07.667 --> 00:09:10.501
It felt insane, but, no, I was there.

00:09:10.501 --> 00:09:11.834
-Alright. -I was with him.

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:13.400
-Well, I'm happy you were there.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.567
I am happy you were here.

00:09:14.567 --> 00:09:16.000
It's always so great to see you, Adam.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.734
Adam Pally! "Who Invited Charlie?"

00:09:18.734 --> 00:09:20.701
is in theaters and on demand February 3rd.

00:09:20.701 --> 00:09:22.634
We'll be right back with more "Late Night."

